# Frontend mission (Nic) — reference-or-nothing

Goal: the site judges wish NASA had shipped. 14k teams. Fall-on-the-floor wow.

## Every loop MUST

1. Invent **one phenomenal, outside-the-box idea** (would impress a strong critic, not just “nice UI”).
2. Write it in `docs/win-progress.md` before coding (“This loop’s wow: …”).
3. Ship that idea end-to-end.
4. Cosmetic polish is **allowed** (and encouraged) **only as support** for the wow — never as the whole loop.

## Bar for “phenomenal”

Ask: if Claude / a NASA judge saw this for 10 seconds, would they **stop scrolling**?
- New perception of motion, cinematic mission experience, discovery mechanic, shareable moment, immersive stage…
- Not: another settings row, another synonym for “Play”.

## Attitude

Break conventions. Prefer bold product bets over safe dashboards. Under-estimate % in `win-progress.md`.
